// A `#run` calling an **imported** procedure (ADR-0069 §1) — the first W4 sub-wave, and the first time
// this compiler executes a library procedure *while compiling*.
//
// Before this, `#run area(...)` on an imported `area` reported
//
//     error[E0230]: compile-time evaluation failed: internal compiler error:
//     no routine for file 1 proc 11
//
// which is compiler internals shown to a user who wrote a reasonable program. The cause was one line:
// `file_consts` put *its own file's* bytecode in the comptime program and no other, so an imported
// callee had none. `run_main` and `build` already walk every reachable file for exactly this reason.
//
// Three things here are worth checking rather than assuming:
//
//   * an imported procedure is **callable at compile time**, and the value lands in a constant;
//   * the callee takes the implicit **context** (ADR-0057 §4), which the thunk must pass — an imported
//     callee answered "no context" through a `target.file == self.file` gate that was correct only while
//     a cross-file `#run` was impossible, and the interpreter then said "called a procedure taking 2
//     arguments with 1". A silent argument-count mismatch, so putting the bytecode in the program was
//     not enough on its own;
//   * the imported callee takes a **struct parameter**, so the cross-file path carries an aggregate
//     rather than only scalars.
//
// **No `#import "Basic"`**, matching every other file in this directory: its harnesses resolve against
// `tests/corpus/modules` only, so importing the bundled standard library is E0210 there. The values are
// therefore accumulated and compared rather than exited on — `valid/056` is the file that makes a `#run`
// observable to the differential harness.
#import "Shapes";

/// A rectangle measured at **compile time**, through a procedure in another file.
///
/// `area` lives in `Shapes`, not here — that is the whole point of this file.
AREA :: #run area(make(3, 4));

/// A second one, so the cross-file path is exercised more than once in a single round of const-eval.
WIDE :: #run area(make(10, 2));

/// Local, because a `#run` cannot use a struct literal yet: the aggregate is assembled by a procedure in
/// *this* file and handed to the imported one, which exercises the cross-file argument path.
make :: (w: s64, h: s64) -> Rect {
    r: Rect;
    r.w = w;
    r.h = h;
    return r;
}

main :: () {
    n := 0;

    // 3 * 4, computed while compiling.
    if AREA == 12 {
        n = n + 1;
    }
    // 10 * 2, likewise.
    if WIDE == 20 {
        n = n + 2;
    }
    // And the module's own constant still crosses, so this file does not accidentally test only `#run`.
    if SHAPES_VERSION == 1 {
        n = n + 4;
    }

    // Accumulated rather than exited on, per the directory's convention above.
    if n == 7 {
        return;
    }
}
